  </div>

  <p>
    Still thinking about government routes? See
    <a href="/blog/government-jobs/psu-jobs-after-engineering-india/">PSU jobs after engineering</a> and
    <a href="/blog/government-jobs/government-jobs-after-engineering-india/">government jobs after engineering</a>.
    If you are comparing engineering itself with another stream, or a family member is, start with
    <a href="/blog/stream-selection/engineering-vs-other-streams-which-is-better-career-india/">engineering versus other streams</a> and
    <a href="/blog/career-options/is-engineering-still-a-good-career-in-india/">is engineering still a good career in India</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="own-work">Freelance, consulting or startup: the sales basics engineers skip</h2>

  <p>
    Engineers learn to build, not to be found and trusted. Every route on the ownership side has a plain question behind it: who pays, and how do they find and trust you? Learn these six basics before you spend a rupee on a logo or a website.
  </p>

  <ol class="rich-list">
    {salesSteps.map((s) => (
      <li><strong>{s.title}</strong> {s.body}</li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <p>
    Who pays depends on the route. In freelance and consulting work it is a small firm, an agency or a former employer. In a startup it is a customer. In a PSU or government post it is the employer, so the sales layer matters mainly for the side route or the move that comes after. Nothing here promises income. It makes your first conversations less random.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    If you earn outside a job, check GST and Udyam rules on the official portals, because thresholds and rules change. For a deeper start, see
    <a href="/blog/freelancing-business/how-to-start-freelancing/">how to start freelancing</a> and
    <a href="/blog/freelancing-business/consulting-as-a-career-india-how-to-get-into-consulting/">consulting as a career</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI: where it helps and where it takes the first rung</h2>

  <p>
    AI is not one threat. It is changing different layers at different speeds. In 2026, recruiters and analysts quoted in the press linked weaker entry-level hiring partly to automation and partly to a cautious market, so do not assume AI is the only cause.
  </p>

  <div class="skill-levels">
    {aiRows.map((row) => (
      <div class="skill-level">
        <div class={`skill-level__header skill-level__header--${row.level}`}>{row.head}</div>
        <ul class="skill-list">
          {row.items.map((item) => (
            <li><span class={`skill-dot skill-dot--${row.level}`}></span>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    Build in stages. Start by using AI to speed up the routine part of your own branch's work while you check every output. Later, as tools mature, move toward designing the workflow, directing automations and owning the final judgment. Tool familiarity is not proof. A result you can show is.
  </p>

  <h2 id="weak-signal">Low CGPA, backlogs or a weak college: honest paths</h2>

  <p>
    A weak academic signal is one gate, not the whole market. Backlogs, a low CGPA and a college with a weak name are three different problems, so treat them separately.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">What to repair first</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Active backlogs: clear them first. Without the certificate, most routes are closed.</li>
      <li>Low CGPA: it cannot be changed now, so build a stronger signal beside it with shipped work, a cleaner profile and a narrower target role.</li>
      <li>Weak college name: widen your list to startups, small firms and proof-first employers, and use referrals more than mass applications.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      Do not hide the marks. Give a one-line honest explanation and then show better work. A narrow first target and one clean proof piece usually beat a wide search.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Routes where marks matter less</div>
      <ul>
        <li>A skill-led switch with a deployed project.</li>
        <li>Freelance and small-firm work where your output is the test.</li>
        <li>GATE, where the exam score is what counts for an M.Tech seat.</li>
        <li>UPSC civil services, which accepts any degree.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Routes where marks matter more</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Campus drives with a CGPA cut-off.</li>
        <li>PSUs that check a minimum aggregate in their own notice.</li>
        <li>Competitive MBA and MS admissions, where the profile is read closely.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    A student from a smaller college has more company than it feels like. See
    <a href="/blog/career-options/tier-2-college-student-career-options-india/">career options for tier-2 college students</a>
    and
    <a href="/blog/job-search/campus-vs-off-campus-placement-india/">campus versus off-campus placement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="skill-stack">The skill stack that works on every route</h2>

  <p>
    Whatever you pick, build the same three layers: one core skill, one multiplier skill and visible proof. A civil engineer who knows BIM (core) and can build a clear cost dashboard (multiplier) and shows one real project (proof) is easier to hire, or to pay, than ten certificates.
  </p>

  <div class="stack-grid">
    <div class="stack-card">
      <div class="stack-card__label">Learn it cheaply</div>
      <p>YouTube, official documents, NPTEL-style open courses and a few well-reviewed low-cost courses cover most of what you need. Judge each course on its instructor, last update, exercises and feedback. Pay only for something free material cannot give you, such as expert feedback, accountability or a credential the target role truly needs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stack-card">
      <div class="stack-card__label">Show it early</div>
      <p>Pick one platform that suits your work, such as GitHub, LinkedIn, a portfolio page or a case-note folder, and keep it current. One platform used well beats five abandoned profiles. Where work is confidential, use anonymised case notes or simulations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stack-card">
      <div class="stack-card__label">Explain it well</div>
      <p>Clear English, written and spoken, opens interviews, clients and senior people. Add basic AI and data comfort in your own branch, and meet people who already work where you want to be. Choose a route that fits how you want to work, including remote or hybrid.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

